{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כי מראש צרים אראנו", :translit "ki meroshei tzurim er'enu", :gloss "for from the top of rocks I see him"} {:he "אראנו", :translit "er'enu", :gloss "I see him"} {:he "הצורים", :translit "hatzurim", :gloss "the rocks"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: אראנו reinterpreted as 'I see that they were created' linked to בריאה"}], :frame {:text "Balaam's prophecy in Numbers 23:9 is part of his first oracle over Israel. The verse reads: 'For from the top of the rocks I see him.' The Ba'al HaTurim reads the language of seeing as referring to Israel's preexistence in the divine plan, a motif found in sources that speak of entities conceived before creation. The Patriarchs are described as hewn from a rock and quarried from a pit in Isaiah 51:1–2.", :sources ["Isaiah 51:1–2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "כי מראש", :translit "ki merosh", :gloss "for from the top"} {:he "הר המוריה", :translit "har hamoriyah", :gloss "Mount Moriah"} {:he "מראש צרים", :translit "merosh tzurim", :gloss "from the top of rocks"} {:he "מזכות אבות", :translit "mezechut avot", :gloss "from the merit of the fathers"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "כי מראש", :b "הר המוריה"} {:kind :gematria, :a "מראש צרים", :b "מזכות אבות"}], :frame {:text "Mount Moriah is identified as the site of the binding of Isaac in Genesis 22:2 and as the location of the Temple in 2 Chronicles 3:1. The merit of the Patriarchs is a recurrent theme in biblical interpretation; God remembers the covenant with the Patriarchs in Leviticus 26:42 and Micah 7:20. The rocks from which Balaam sees Israel are thus linked to the Temple mount and to the ancestral merit that protects their descendants.", :sources ["Genesis 22:2" "2 Chronicles 3:1" "Leviticus 26:42" "Micah 7:20"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מגבעות", :translit "miggva'ot", :gloss "from the hills"} {:he "הן האמהות", :translit "hen ha'emahot", :gloss "these are the matriarchs"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "מגבעות", :b "הן האמהות"}], :frame {:text "Just as the rocks were identified with the Patriarchs in the preceding comment, the hills are now linked to the Matriarchs. The pairing of patriarchs with rocks and matriarchs with hills echoes Isaiah 51:1, which calls Israel to look to the rock from which they were hewn and the quarry from which they were dug, immediately followed by reference to Abraham and Sarah in Isaiah 51:2.", :sources ["Isaiah 51:1–2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לבדד", :translit "levadad", :gloss "alone"} {:he "עם לבדד ישכון", :translit "am levadad yishkon", :gloss "a people alone shall dwell"} {:he "שכני לבדד", :translit "shachnei levadad", :gloss "my neighbor alone"} {:he "כי אתה ה' לבדד", :translit "ki atah hashem levadad", :gloss "for You YHWH alone"} {:he "לבטח תושיבני", :translit "levetach toshivenu", :gloss "securely will You settle me"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["עם לבדד ישכון" "שכני לבדד" "כי אתה ה' לבדד"]}], :frame {:text "Balaam's prophecy is understood in midrashic sources as touching on Israel's future redemption. The three occurrences of לבדד are each linked to a dimension of redemption: Numbers 23:9 is Balaam's own oracle; Deuteronomy 33:28 speaks of Israel dwelling securely alone; and Psalms 4:9, 'For You alone, O YHWH, make me dwell in safety,' is read as God never being angry during the era of settlement. The Talmud states that God swore never to be angry again after the destruction of the First Temple, linking divine forbearance to Israel's secure dwelling.", :sources ["Numbers 23:9" "Deuteronomy 33:28" "Psalms 4:9" "Sanhedrin 105a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לבדד ישכון", :translit "levadad yishkon", :gloss "alone shall dwell"} {:he "שי״ן דישכון", :translit "shin dishkon", :gloss "shin of yishkon"} {:he "ז' תגין", :translit "shiv'ah tagin", :gloss "seven tagin"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Seven tagin on the shin of ישכון correspond to seven nations"}], :frame {:text "The verse Deuteronomy 7:1 lists seven nations whom Israel will dispossess in the land: the Hittite, Girgashite, Amorite, Canaanite, Perizzite, Hivite, and Jebusite. The unusual ornamental tagin on letters in the Torah are treated by the Ba'al HaTurim as carrying symbolic meaning; here, seven crowns on the shin of 'shall dwell' signal Israel's dwelling in a land of seven nations.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 7:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לבדד", :translit "levadad", :gloss "alone"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "לבדד", :b "מ׳"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud records a view that the land of Israel is forty by forty mil, drawing on the spies' forty-day reconnaissance in Numbers 13:25. The forty days of spying correspond to the breadth of the land. The Ba'al HaTurim links the numerical value of לבדד, which equals forty, to this measurement.", :sources ["Numbers 13:25" "Sotah 34b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לבדד ישכן", :translit "levadad yishkan", :gloss "alone shall dwell"} {:he "ת״כ", :translit "tak", :gloss "420"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "לבדד ישכן", :b "ת״כ"}], :frame {:text "The Second Temple period is traditionally calculated at 420 years, as stated in the Talmud, following the chronology of the Persian and Hellenistic eras. The Ba'al HaTurim links this number to the gematria of 'לבדד ישכן,' reading Balaam's prophecy as an allusion to the span of the Second Temple.", :sources ["Avodah Zarah 9a" "Yoma 54a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ל", :translit "lamed", :gloss "L (alone)"} {:he "בדד ישכן", :translit "vadad yishkan", :gloss "(with ל removed) alone shall dwell"} {:he "בימי משיח", :translit "bimei mashiach", :gloss "in the days of the Messiah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ל בדד ישכן", :b "בימי משיח"}], :frame {:text "Balaam's prophecy is understood in the Sifre as containing an allusion to the end of days. The phrase 'a people alone' (Numbers 23:9) is read as pointing to Israel's ultimate isolation in holiness in the messianic era. The Ba'al HaTurim extracts the letter ל alone and through gematria links it to the messianic period.", :sources ["Numbers 23:9" "Sifre Numbers 131"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: אראנו reinterpreted as 'I see that they were created' linked to בריאה", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "כי מראש", :a-value 571, :b "הר המוריה", :b-value 471, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:a-value 881, :b-value 882, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "מזכות אבות", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "מראש צרים"} {:kind :gematria, :a "מגבעות", :a-value 521, :b "הן האמהות", :b-value 512, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["עם לבדד ישכון" "שכני לבדד" "כי אתה ה' לבדד"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "עם לבדד ישכון", :refs ["Numbers 23:9"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "שכני לבדד", :refs ["Micah 7:14"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כי אתה ה' לבדד", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Seven tagin on the shin of ישכון correspond to seven nations", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "לבדד", :a-value 40, :b "מ׳", :b-value 40, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :gematria, :a "לבדד ישכן", :a-value 420, :b "ת״כ", :b-value 420, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :gematria, :a "ל בדד ישכן", :a-value 420, :b "בימי משיח", :b-value 420, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-13T00:33:56.474987654Z", :model "glm-5.2"}